@page "/help"

@using Simplifiarr.Core.Utilities

<PageTitle>Help - Simplifiarr</PageTitle>

<PageHeader Title="Help"
            Subtitle="Simple tools for a complex system. What each page is for, and how Simplifiarr keeps your files safe." />

@* Scrolled by hand: Blazor's own navigation doesn't scroll to a #section. *@
<nav class="help-contents" aria-label="On this page">
    <a href="help#start" onclick="document.getElementById('start').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'}); return false;">Getting started</a>
    <a href="help#scan" onclick="document.getElementById('scan').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'}); return false;">Scanning</a>
    @foreach (var group in Groups)
    {
        <a href="@($"help#{group.Id}")" onclick="@($"document.getElementById('{group.Id}').scrollIntoView({{behavior:'smooth'}}); return false;")">@group.Title</a>
    }
    <a href="help#safety" onclick="document.getElementById('safety').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'}); return false;">Safety net</a>
    <a href="help#settings" onclick="document.getElementById('settings').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'}); return false;">Settings</a>
    <a href="help#questions" onclick="document.getElementById('questions').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'}); return false;">Questions</a>
</nav>

@* ------------------------------------------------------------------ Start *@

<section class="section" id="start">
    <h2 class="section-title">Getting started</h2>

    <div class="panel help-panel">
        <p>
            A <strong>hardlink</strong> lets one file appear in two folders while taking up the
            space of one. Simplifiarr uses that so a download can keep seeding while the same
            file sits in your library - no second copy.
        </p>

        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>
                <strong>Add your drives.</strong>
                In <a href="settings">Settings</a>, add one entry per drive with whichever library
                folders it has. Hardlinks only work within one drive, so the simplest setup is one
                <em>downloads drive</em> where everything new arrives: pick it at the top of the Drives
                tab, and Storage moves finished titles to the other drives as it fills. Or give each
                drive its own downloads folder.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Connect your apps (optional).</strong>
                Your torrent client, Radarr, Sonarr, Prowlarr and Jellyfin each unlock more. Simplifiarr
                works without any of them.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Press Scan.</strong>
                It's at the top of every page.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Look at Home.</strong>
                It shows what the scan found and links to anything that needs you.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

@* ------------------------------------------------------------------- Scan *@

<section class="section" id="scan">
    <h2 class="section-title">Scanning</h2>

    <div class="panel help-panel">
        <p>
            There is one <strong>Scan</strong> button, at the top of every page. It reads every drive
            in Settings and refreshes every list in Simplifiarr at once. It runs on the server, so you
            can move between pages or close the browser and it carries on. <strong>Stop</strong>
            ends it early; lists keep what they had.
        </p>

        <p>
            To have Scan run by itself, every few hours or once a day, use
            <a href="settings">Settings</a>, under Scanning. It can also search for cross-seeds
            afterwards. Automatic scans only find things: nothing is linked, moved or deleted until
            you press a button.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
            The first scan of a large library takes a while, because each video's resolution is read
            once. Later scans only look at what changed and are much quicker.
        </p>
    </div>

    <p class="cell-note">
        A few pages search elsewhere and have their own button instead:
        Size Reduction and Cross-Seed (your indexers) and Posters (Jellyfin).
    </p>
</section>

@* ------------------------------------------------------------- Tool groups *@
@* The same groups, in the same order, as the menu. *@

@foreach (var group in Groups)
{
    <section class="section" id="@group.Id">
        <h2 class="section-title">@group.Title</h2>

        <div class="panel">
            @foreach (var page in group.Pages)
            {
                <HelpRow Page="page" />
            }
        </div>
    </section>
}

@* -------------------------------------------------------------- Safety net *@

<section class="section" id="safety">
    <h2 class="section-title">Safety net</h2>

    <div class="panel help-panel">
        <p>Simplifiarr is built so a mistake can be undone:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                It deletes a file outright only when its bytes are kept somewhere else (a moved title's checked
                copy, a download your library has byte for byte), when you delete it from Quarantine, or when a
                Rolling rule is set to delete for good. Everything else it removes goes to Quarantine, on the
                same drive it came from, so nothing is copied and the space comes back when you empty it.
            </li>
            <li>The only time it copies between drives is a <a href="storage">Storage</a> move you asked for. Each file is checked against the original before the old copy is removed, and titles move one at a time.</li>
            <li>Anything taken out of a library goes to <a href="quarantine">Quarantine</a> first. Restore puts it back; Delete removes it for good.</li>
            <li>A hardlink is only counted as done once Simplifiarr has checked it really is the same file.</li>
            <li>Cross-seeds and rebuilt torrents are only offered once every piece has been checked against your files, and are added to your torrent client stopped.</li>
            <li>Anything that changes files asks you to confirm first.</li>
            <li>The only change Simplifiarr makes to a torrent already in your torrent client is Move Seeds, one torrent at a time when you ask. It is undone if the client's check doesn't pass.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="panel mt-3">
        @foreach (var page in SafetyPages)
        {
            <HelpRow Page="page" />
        }
    </div>
</section>

@* --------------------------------------------------------------- Settings *@

<section class="section" id="settings">
    <h2 class="section-title">Settings</h2>

    <div class="panel help-panel">
        <dl class="help-terms">
            <dt>Drives</dt>
            <dd>
                <em>New downloads land on</em> picks the downloads drive: the one your torrent client
                saves to and Radarr, Sonarr and Seerr add new titles to. It is kept clear, and the other
                drives are overflow drives that only need libraries. The Setup page checks your apps
                fit this, and changes what it can.
                One entry per drive. <em>Downloads folder</em> is where finished torrents land;
                the library folders are where your organised Movies, TV, Books, Audiobooks, Music and
                Comics live. Leave out any you don't have. Movies, TV and books can simply share the main
                downloads folder: everything under it is looked at, and movies are told from episodes by
                their names. Giving them their own folders is optional; a movie downloads folder is then
                only searched for movies, and a TV one only for TV. Audiobooks, music and comics each need their
                own downloads folder, because their files can't be told apart by content alone.
                Each path says whether it exists as you type. Starting fresh?
                <code>scripts\new-media-folders.ps1 -Drive D</code> in the Simplifiarr folder
                creates the whole set for a drive and prints what to type here.
            </dd>

            <dt>Connections</dt>
            <dd>
                Your torrent client, qBittorrent for now (what is still seeding), Radarr and Sonarr (exact titles, genres and episode
                numbers; Copies uses their folders and folder formats; Storage updates them when titles move or are deleted), Prowlarr (searching your
                indexers), Jellyfin (Collections, Posters and watch history), Seerr (who asked for each title) and an optional fanart.tv key (more
                artwork). Each has a Test button.
            </dd>

            <dt>Storage</dt>
            <dd class="mb-0">
                Where Quarantine, History and cross-seed links are kept, and where to find ffprobe.
                Simplifiarr's own settings are in <code>@AppPaths.SettingsFile</code>.
            </dd>
        </dl>
    </div>
</section>

@* -------------------------------------------------------------- Questions *@

<section class="section" id="support">
    <h2 class="section-title">Something not working?</h2>

    <div class="panel storage-box">
        <a href="support">Logs &amp; support</a> downloads Simplifiarr's logs as one zip, with API keys,
        passwords and (by default) your titles taken out, and opens a GitHub issue or an email to send it with.
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="questions">
    <h2 class="section-title">Questions</h2>

    <div class="panel">
        @foreach (var (question, answer) in Questions)
        {
            <details class="help-question">
                <summary>@question</summary>
                <p>@answer</p>
            </details>
        }
    </div>
</section>

@code
{
    public sealed record HelpPage(
        string Href,
        string Icon,
        string Name,
        string Text);

    private static readonly HelpPage[] TorrentPages =
    [
        new("move-seeds", "truck", "Move Seeds",
            "Torrents seeding from one drive while Sonarr or Radarr copied them into a library on another. Moving the seed to the library's drive leaves one shared copy. The torrent client checks every piece before the old copy is deleted, and the torrent is left paused."),
        new("cross-seed", "share", "Cross-Seed",
            "Finds other torrents of files you already seed, so you can seed them on more trackers without downloading anything."),
        new("torrent-rebuilder", "hammer", "Torrent Rebuilder",
            "Rebuilds one torrent from files already in your library, even renamed ones, so it can seed straight away.")
    ];

    private static readonly HelpPage[] SpacePages =
    [
        new("copies", "copy", "Copies",
            "Everything on your drives more than once, every drive checked together, and each download in one tab only. Same file twice: a download with the same bytes as a library file is deleted when nothing seeds it (after every byte is compared), or the library copy becomes a second name for it while it seeds. More than one version: the same movie, episode, book or album as different files; you pick which to keep and the rest go to Quarantine. Not in your library: link finished downloads in without copying, with Sonarr's own folder names for new seasons."),
        new("storage", "device-hdd", "Storage",
            "How full each drive is, and what fills it. The downloads drive (or, without one, each protected drive) is kept under a limit you set: titles nobody watches move off it to the overflow drive with the most free space, one at a time, telling Radarr or Sonarr the new folder. Titles a torrent seeds, shows still airing, and titles added recently or being watched stay put. A moved title's old folder, and any leftover download name of its files, are deleted once the copy is checked, so the space really comes back. Also lists titles worth a look, which can be deleted through Radarr or Sonarr."),
        new("junk-cleanup", "trash3", "Junk",
            "Sample clips, checksum and tracker files, and stray images left in your libraries. You choose what counts as junk, and which kinds of picture to keep."),
        new("size-reduction", "file-earmark-zip", "Size Reduction",
            "Smaller releases of films and episodes you have, found on your indexers, kept to the encodes you accept. Download one and it is swapped in for yours.")
    ];

    private static readonly HelpPage[] FixPages =
    [
        new("folder-fixer", "signpost-split", "Folder Fixer",
            "Movies and shows Radarr or Sonarr point at a folder that no longer exists, usually because it was moved by hand: points them at where the folder is now. Also finds seasons split across two folders (Season 6 and Season 06), explains why, and merges them."),
        new("playback-errors", "exclamation-octagon", "Playback Errors",
            "Files your media server may not be able to open: blocked by Windows, permissions it can't read, still packed in an archive, empty, unfinished, or badly named. Several can be fixed in one click."),
        new("music", "music-note-beamed", "Music",
            "Tidies music libraries: tracks not in an album folder, several albums in one folder, an album split across folders, the same album twice, leftovers and broken tracks. Converts tracks to MP3, AAC, Opus or FLAC, keeping their tags and cover art.")
    ];

    private static readonly HelpPage[] JellyfinPages =
    [
        new("posters", "image", "Posters",
            "Choose the poster, backdrop, logo and other artwork for any film, show, season or collection in Jellyfin from everything found online, or drop in your own. You pick which kinds of picture to work with."),
        new("collections", "collection", "Collections",
            "Group anything in your libraries and send the group to Jellyfin as a collection. Sending again only changes what changed.")
    ];

    private static readonly HelpPage[] AutomaticPages =
    [
        new("rolling-shows", "tv", "Rolling Shows",
            "For daily and weekly shows: keep only the newest episodes, the last so many days, or the current season, and let older ones go as new ones arrive. Can wait until an episode is watched. Sonarr stops looking for each episode before it is deleted. Preview before turning a rule on; runs on every Scan, or the moment Sonarr imports an episode with its webhook."),
        new("rolling-movies", "film", "Rolling Movies",
            "Rules that delete movies by themselves. Pick which movies by Radarr tag, who asked for them in Seerr, folder, or one by one; they go a number of days after being watched (by whoever asked, anyone, or people you pick), after months unwatched, a number of days after arriving, or when their drive is over its limit. Each leaves Radarr, and Seerr so it can be asked for again. Favorites, movies you kept on Storage and the keep tag are never deleted. Preview before turning a rule on; runs on every Scan.")
    ];

    private sealed record HelpGroup(string Id, string Title, HelpPage[] Pages);

    private static readonly HelpGroup[] Groups =
    [
        new("torrents", "Torrents & seeding", TorrentPages),
        new("space", "Free up space", SpacePages),
        new("fix", "Fix & tidy", FixPages),
        new("jellyfin", "Jellyfin", JellyfinPages),
        new("automatic", "Automatic", AutomaticPages)
    ];

    private static readonly HelpPage[] SafetyPages =
    [
        new("setup", "ui-checks", "Setup",
            "Checks that your torrent client, Radarr, Sonarr and Seerr fit how Simplifiarr works: new torrents saved on the downloads drive, new titles added to a library there, each title already elsewhere downloading to its own drive (by its tag), and imports hardlinked. Fixes what it safely can with one click, and says how to change the rest yourself. When Storage moves a title, its tag moves with it."),
        new("quarantine", "box-seam", "Quarantine",
            "Everything Simplifiarr took out of a library, waiting for you to restore or delete it."),
        new("history", "clock-history", "History",
            "Every change Simplifiarr has made on disk, newest first."),
        new("ignored", "eye-slash", "Ignored",
            "Things you've told Simplifiarr to stop suggesting. Un-ignore one to see it again.")
    ];

    private static readonly (string Question, string Answer)[] Questions =
    [
        ("Why can't Simplifiarr link a download on one drive into a library on another?",
         "Hardlinks only work within one drive. Linking across drives would mean copying the file, which is exactly what Simplifiarr exists to avoid. Download to the drive the library is on."),
        ("I deleted the download - is my library copy gone too?",
         "No. Both names point at the same data, and it stays until the last name is deleted. Deleting either one leaves the other working."),
        ("Something I expected isn't on a list.",
         "Lists show what the last scan found. Press Scan, and check the item isn't on the Ignored page and its folder is in Settings."),
        ("Why does a film show 'resolution not known'?",
         "Simplifiarr reads it with ffprobe. If ffprobe isn't installed or can't be found, set its location under Settings, Storage."),
        ("Does Simplifiarr change Radarr, Sonarr or Jellyfin?",
         "It only reads Radarr and Sonarr. In Jellyfin it only changes collections it made and pictures you choose. In your torrent client it adds torrents stopped, and moves a seed only when you press Move."),
        ("Where are the logs?",
         $"In {AppPaths.LogsDirectory}. They are the first place to look if something goes wrong.")
    ];
}
